      "message": "Is this true? Can I really call `select_next_stage` with *any* slice and get a valid response?\n\n(It appears that I\u0027m being stricter than whoever the previous unsafe reviewer was in this file, as for the same reason, `main_wrapper` and `start` at a minimum are supposed to be unsafe - the rule is supposed to be that if you would do something illegal (in this case create a function pointer that\u0027s not guaranteed to point at a function with appropriate ABI and executability) on some inputs, you should mark the function as `unsafe`, and document what needs to be true. In this case, that condition would probably be something like \"`kernel` points to a kernel image following spec X\", and then eventually up the callchain, you\u0027d say something like \"We just checked the signature on this, and we only sign things that follow spec X (or \"the user asserted this follows spec X\"), so this will be fine\")",
